# NOTICE — science
## Imported content
Imported upstream `up:science-research` **in full** (see
`NOTICE.md at the package root` for its path), excluding only three `.git`
directories (38M, 2681 files).
The content of **every repository below belongs to other authors**. The upstream
skill added the router (`SKILL.md`), index (`references/`), and regeneration
scripts (`scripts/`). Our additions were this NOTICE and contract tests (`tests/`).
| Tag | Repository | Skill count | Pinned commit | License |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `kdense` | [K-Dense-AI/scientific-agent-skills](https://github.com/K-Dense-AI/scientific-agent-skills) | 159 | `36d8f13` (2026-08-24) | **MIT** |
| `gdm` | [google-deepmind/science-skills](https://github.com/google-deepmind/science-skills) | 38 | `0b42509` (2026-07-07) | **Apache-2.0** |
| `academic` | [Imbad0202/academic-research-skills](https://github.com/Imbad0202/academic-research-skills) | 4 | `9469fc4` (2026-08-27) | **CC BY-NC 4.0** |
| `kwp` | [anthropics/knowledge-work-plugins](https://github.com/anthropics/knowledge-work-plugins) | 2 | `d900840` (2026-11-03) | **Apache-2.0** |
The complete original license texts remain in their repositories:
`repos/kdense/LICENSE.md`, `repos/gdm/LICENSE`, `repos/academic/LICENSE`, and
`repos/kwp/LICENSE`.
`kwp` was added later and **in part**, not with the original import. Of
`anthropics/knowledge-work-plugins` @ `d900840716eb262e1feb17c6f4406c9ce0e06bcf`
only `data/skills/validate-data/SKILL.md` and
`data/skills/statistical-analysis/SKILL.md` were copied, byte-identical, with the
root `LICENSE` (the same Apache-2.0 text as `data/LICENSE`).
`repos/kwp/UPSTREAM.sha256` was written from the fetched clone before any edit.
`validate-data` links to the plugin's `CONNECTORS.md`, which was not imported; that
line points at tools this skill does not connect and can be ignored.
Four `kdense` children, `docx`, `pdf`, `pptx` and `xlsx`, are not included. Each
carried its own `LICENSE.txt` (© 2025 Anthropic, PBC, all rights reserved) that
forbids redistribution, which overrides the repository's MIT license for those
directories. Office documents are handled by `office-documents`; the kdense count
above is the 159 remaining children.
## academic has a noncommercial condition: read before use
`repos/academic` uses **CC BY-NC 4.0**. It is Cheng-I Wu's personal project, as
its `NOTICE.md` states.
**NC prohibits commercial use.** This condition and attribution remain in force
after public packaging. Using the four `academic` skills **directly for commercial
outputs** may fall outside the license. Assess this before using them for paid work,
such as procurement proposals. `tests/run_tests.py` checks that this notice remains.
`kdense` (MIT), `gdm` (Apache-2.0) and `kwp` (Apache-2.0) do not have that restriction.
## Why vendor the content instead of retaining pointers
The routing table points to 203 skills. Pointers would require upstream files on
every user's machine. Team members installing the plugin do not have those files.
The cost is 38M of additional repository content and **manual tracking of upstream updates**. Upstream used `git pull` followed by `rebuild-index.py`; the import no
longer supports that path. The `scripts/` directory is preserved, so clone upstream
again and run the scripts when needed.
## Rewritten, not imported: problem selection
`references/problem-selection.md` is local text. It restates, in new words, the
problem-selection stages of `TaewiKim/autoresearchlab` @
`80c5d2180094cade4446c32d35a2fb60fdedb105` (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Taewi Kim),
read from `native/researchlab-harness/src/labdirector/problem_selection/`. No code
or prompt text was copied, so nothing from that repository is under `repos/`.
